				<td style="WIDTH: 15px" width="15"></td>
				<td align="left" class="TextMain">
					<center><h2>Rules And Conduct For Officers</h2></center>
					
					In essence, the word officer primarily means certain qualities about a person’s 
					approach and involvement. <BR><BR>
					1. Play time- On-line a lot and visible to 
					others in the guild.<BR>
					2. Attitude- An even temper and a voice of reason. An 
					officer sets an example for the rest of the guild.<BR>
					3. Honesty- Lack of 
					deceptiveness and a willingness to admit mistakes and say ‘I was wrong’.<BR>
					4. 
					Fairness- Patience to listen with a desire to see a situation thru another 
					persons eyes.<BR>
					5. Respect- Valuing a person for the sake of who they are and 
					what they believe.<BR>
					6. Loyalty- Support the guild leader and officers. <BR>
					7. 
					Tolerance- Despite personal opinion, acceptance that others have different 
					personalities and play styles.<BR>
					8. Unselfish- A true desire to see others 
					succeed more than yourself.<BR>
					9. Commitment- Betterment of this guild and its 
					members by participation, coordinating, and running events. <BR>
					10. Involvement- 
					Spending time with a variety of others in the guild, both in game and on the 
					message boards. <BR>
					11. Presence- Initiative to speak up in guild chat, but not 
					so much that it is overbearing.<BR>
					12. Trust- A willingness to follow blindly, 
					if you must, because you respect a person’s judgement.<BR>
					13. Discretion- An appreciation that some things are better left unsaid. <BR><BR>
					
					An officership has nothing to do with friendship or winning the Mr/Miss Congeniality contest. It is 
					hoped that the officer ranks will provide the stability and core for the rest of 
					the guild. These are the folks who will not let an incident or two tarnish their 
					image of the guild. The officers are here for the long term and have the 
					patience and tolerance to gut it out through the tough times. <BR><BR>
					
					Officers as valued consultants. They are the machinery that makes things happen. They 
					have a voice in Garaddor’s ear and influence on his decisions.<BR><BR>
					
					Officers are not better than anyone else in the guild and should not be pulling rank and 
					using the title as some kind of club on the membership. First and foremost we 
					are mentors, teachers, and peers with our guildmates. We strive to set an 
					example that everyone else in the guild would be proud of. In fact this applies 
					to those outside our guild as well. Our reputation as individuals and as a guild 
					is a very precious treasure that must be cultivated on a daily basis.
					<BR><BR><br>
				</td>
